The Mercedes-Benz CLS 400d refers to the C257 generation (2018-2023). It was available with slightly different power outputs (330 PS / 326 hp or 340 PS / 335 hp) depending on the year and market. I will use the specs for the 340 PS / 335 hp version as it is commonly cited.

**Key Data Extracted:**
*   **Engine:** 2.9L Inline 6 Turbo Diesel (OM656)
*   **HP:** 335 HP (250 kW / 340 PS) (Also 330 HP / 326 PS / 243 kW on later models) - Using 335 HP.
*   **Torque:** 700 Nm (516 lb-ft)
*   **Cylinder Count:** 6
*   **Engine Displacement:** 2.9L (2925-2927 cm³)
*   **0-60 mph:** ~4.7-5.0 seconds (0-100 km/h is 5.0-5.2s) - Using 4.8s.
*   **Top Speed:** 155 mph (250 km/h) (Electronically limited)
*   **Drive Type:** 4MATIC (All-wheel drive)
*   **Transmission Type:** 9-speed Automatic (9G-Tronic)
*   **Size (Length):** ~4988-4996 mm (196.4-196.7 inches) - Using 4996mm.
*   **Wheelbase:** ~2939 mm (115.7 inches)
*   **Body Style:** 4-door Coupe/Saloon
*   **Seats:** 5 (Some sources mention 4, but 5 is standard for C257) - Using 5.
*   **Cargo Space:** ~490-520 Litres (~17.3-18.4 cu ft) - Using 520L (18.4 cu ft).
*   **Rear Space:** Limited due to coupe roofline. Headroom ~927mm (36.5 inches). Legroom not explicitly found, but generally less than E-Class.
*   **Ground Clearance_in:** ~93-130 mm (~3.66-5.1 inches) - Using 5 inches (approx 130mm).
*   **Turn Radius_ft:** ~11.2-12.3 meters (~36.7-40.4 ft) - Using 11.9m (39.04 ft).
*   **MPG:** Combined WLTP ~35-42 US mpg (~42-50 UK mpg). Real-world often lower. Using a blend, leaning towards real-world (~35-40 US mpg).
*   **CO2_g_km:** 148-197 g/km (NEDC/WLTP). Using 156 g/km (NEDC) or 178 g/km (WLTP). Using 178 g/km (WLTP) as it's more recent.
*   **Electrification:** Diesel. Some sources mention mild hybrid for other C257 engines, but 400d is typically just diesel.
*   **Electric Range/Charge Speed:** N/A.
*   **Price (New):** Around £60k+ when new (~$75k+). Used prices vary greatly, from ~$12k to ~$53k+ depending on year/mileage. Scoring based on new price range.
*   **Total Cost Estimate 5yr:** Edmunds estimates ~$11.7k over 10 years for maintenance/repairs, higher than average. CarEdge estimates ~$3.8k over 5 years for maintenance/repair, but total ownership cost is high. Score based on high overall cost.
*   **Insurance Group (UK):** Group 50E. Very high.
*   **Maintenance/Repair Risk:** Mercedes maintenance is higher than average. Reliability is below average according to some sources (Consumer Reports 19/100). Known issues with electrical gremlins. Score based on below-average reliability and high cost.
*   **ADAS:** Standard and optional advanced ADAS available, including systems from the S-Class.
*   **Interior/Tech:** Dual 12.3-inch screens, MBUX, Apple CarPlay/Android Auto, high-quality materials, comfort features. Burmester audio available. Wireless charging available.
*   **Prestige:** Mercedes-Benz is high brand prestige. CLS is a step below S-Class but above E-Class (model prestige). 400d is a high-end engine/trim for the CLS (trim prestige).
*   **Ride & Handling:** Comfortable GT car, not focused on sporty handling. Air Body Control (air suspension) optional for enhanced comfort. Steering not especially feelsome. Good refinement.

